---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const updated = "21 September 2026";
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${site.name}`}
  description="How kleinbem.dev handles personal data, including optional sign-in via email/password or Google."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      This site is a static personal / consulting website operated by {site.name} (Co. Cork,
      Ireland). It runs no advertising, no cross-site tracking, and no cookie-based analytics.
      Traffic is measured only in aggregate via Cloudflare Web Analytics (cookieless, no
      client-side storage, no personal data — see &ldquo;Third parties&rdquo; below). The only
      processing that identifies you is the optional <strong class="text-fg">sign-in</strong>
      feature described below, plus standard web-server and CDN access logs.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">Signing in</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Sign-in is entirely optional — the site is fully usable without an account. If you choose
      to sign in, you're taken to <code class="rounded bg-surface px-1 py-0.5 text-[13px]"
        >auth.kleinbem.dev</code
      >, a self-hosted identity service (Authentik) that I operate on my own infrastructure,
      using the industry-standard OpenID Connect protocol. Two ways to sign in are offered:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-3 max-w-2xl list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      <li>
        <strong class="font-medium">Email and password</strong> — created and verified entirely
        on auth.kleinbem.dev. No password is ever seen or stored by kleinbem.dev itself — this
        site never receives it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="font-medium">Google</strong> — you authenticate directly with Google;
        auth.kleinbem.dev never sees your Google password, only the basic profile info Google
        shares back (see &ldquo;Third parties&rdquo; below). No other social providers are
        currently offered.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">
      What is stored
    </h3>
    <ul class="mt-3 max-w-2xl list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      <li>
        On <strong class="font-medium">auth.kleinbem.dev</strong> (not on kleinbem.dev itself):
        your <strong class="font-medium">name</strong> and
        <strong class="font-medium">email address</strong>, plus — for email/password sign-in
        only — a <strong class="font-medium">password hash</strong>. Passwords are never stored
        in plain text; the hash cannot be reversed to recover the original password. Signing in
        with Google creates no password at all.
      </li>
      <li>
        On <strong class="font-medium">kleinbem.dev</strong>, once you've signed in: a single
        cookie containing only your <strong class="font-medium">name</strong> and
        <strong class="font-medium">email address</strong>, cryptographically signed so it
        can't be altered. No password, and no data from auth.kleinbem.dev beyond those two
        fields, ever reaches kleinbem.dev.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">
      Purpose and legal basis
    </h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      This data is used solely to authenticate you and keep you signed in on
      <code class="rounded bg-surface px-1 py-0.5 text-[13px]">kleinbem.dev</code>. The legal
      basis is your consent, given when you choose to sign in (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)), and the
      performance of providing the account feature you requested.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Cookies</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      A single session cookie is set on <code class="rounded bg-surface px-1 py-0.5 text-[13px]"
        >kleinbem.dev</code
      > <em>only after you sign in</em>, valid for up to 30 days, and removed when you sign out.
      There are no advertising or tracking cookies, and no cookies at all until you sign in.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      This cookie doesn't need a consent banner: it's strictly necessary for a feature you
      explicitly asked for by clicking &ldquo;sign in&rdquo;, which is exempt from cookie-consent
      requirements under the ePrivacy Directive (Art. 5(3)). It's not set for anyone who
      doesn't sign in, and it's never used for advertising, tracking, or analytics.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">Third parties</h2>
    <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-5 text-sm sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr]">
      <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Google</dt>
      <dd class="text-fg">
        Used only as an identity provider if you choose to sign in with Google —
        auth.kleinbem.dev requests your basic profile (name, email) from Google, nothing more.
        Google's handling of your data on its own side is governed by
        <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          rel="noopener"
          class="text-heading underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-accent"
          >Google's own privacy policy</a
        >.
      </dd>

      <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Cloudflare</dt>
      <dd class="text-fg">
        CDN and reverse proxy. Access logs record technical data including IP addresses,
        processed on a legitimate-interests basis to deliver and secure the site, and retained
        only briefly. Also provides <strong class="font-medium">Web Analytics</strong>: an
        aggregate traffic measure (page views, referrers, countries, load performance) that
        sets no cookies, stores nothing on your device, and does not build a profile of you or
        track you across sites. And <strong class="font-medium">Turnstile</strong>: a bot-check
        on the contact form, which briefly processes some technical signals from your browser
        (not a CAPTCHA image puzzle) to tell human visitors from automated traffic — see
        <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
          rel="noopener"
          class="text-heading underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-accent"
          >Cloudflare's Turnstile privacy policy</a
        >.
      </dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Your sign-in data is <strong class="font-medium">not</strong> sold, rented, or shared
      with advertisers, and is not used for profiling or automated decision-making.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">
      Retention and your rights
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg">
      Account data is kept until you ask for it to be deleted; expired sessions are removed
      automatically. To delete your account and associated data, or to exercise your rights of
      access, rectification, erasure, portability, or objection under the GDPR, email
      <a
        href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
        class="text-heading underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-accent"
        >{site.email}</a
      >. You may also lodge a complaint with the Irish Data Protection Commission
      (<a
        href="https://www.dataprotection.ie"
        rel="noopener"
        class="text-heading underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-accent"
        >dataprotection.ie</a
      >).
    </p>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">
      This policy may be updated; material changes will be reflected in the &ldquo;last
      updated&rdquo; date above. See also the <a
        href="/impressum"
        class="underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent">Legal Notice</a
      >. Not legal advice.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
